The '''seventeenth series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' will begin on 22 September 2026. It will again be presented by [[Alison Hammond]] and [[Noel Fielding]]. [[Paul Hollywood]] returned as a judge, alongside [[Nigella Lawson]], who replaced [[Prue Leith]] following her departure.<ref>{{cite web |title=Nigella Lawson praised as Bake Off judge as latest contestants announced |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c4gm8npmp4ro |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=8 September 2026 |date=8 September 2026}}</ref>

==Production==
Following the conclusion of the previous series, it was confirmed that ''The Great British Bake Off'' would return for a seventeenth series.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Mensah |first1=Katelyn |title=Great British Bake Off 2026 confirms release date and season 17 cast |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/the-great-british-bake-off-release-date-cast-confirmed-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=8 September 2026}}</ref> In January 2026, [[Prue Leith]] announced she would be stepping down as a judge after nine years and said that "now feels like the right time to step back" [...] There's so much I'd like to do."<ref>{{cite web |title=Dame Prue Leith leaves The Great British Bake Off |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm2j80g4vy3o |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=8 September 2026 |date=21 January 2026}}</ref> Leith also cited feeling unsteady on set as another reason for leaving.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Moss |first1=Molly |title=Prue Leith reveals the real reason why she quit The Great British Bake Off {{!}} Radio Times |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/prue-leith-the-great-british-bake-off-quit-reason-newsupdate/ |website=[[Radio Times]] |access-date=8 September 2026}}</ref> [[Nigella Lawson]] was subsequently announced as her replacement.<ref>{{cite web |title=Bake Off first look: Lashings of Nigella Lawson help everyone rise to the occasion |url=https://www.thetimes.com/culture/tv-radio/article/nigella-lawson-bake-off-first-look-gsbk6hl3t |website=[[The Times]] |access-date=8 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Nigella Lawson to replace Prue Leith on The Great British Bake Off |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgk80pzxkexo |website=[[BBC News]] |access-date=8 September 2026 |date=26 January 2026}}</ref> The first trailer for the series aired in August 2026, featuring hosts [[Alison Hammond]] and [[Noel Fielding]] and judges [[Paul Hollywood]] and Lawson, with each of them holding a fork and battling to be the first to try one of the bakes. Hollywood begins and says "Ooh go on then", before Fielding intercepts by telling him "Not so fast blue eyes". Hammond is next and tells them "Ladies' first" before Lawson coughs and approaches. It is accompanied by the tagline "The bake is back".<ref>{{cite web |last1=Bishop |first1=Holly |title=Nigella Lawson stars in Great British Bake Off trailer ahead of series debut |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/showbiz/nigella-lawson-bake-off-paul-hollywood-b1294570.html |website=[[Evening Standard]] |access-date=8 September 2026 |language=en |date=25 August 2026}}</ref> Prior to the beginning of the series, it was announced that the spin-off ''[[The Great British Bake Off: An Extra Slice]]'' had been axed and would be replaced by another spin off, ''Second Helpings'', hosted by [[Jon Richardson]] and [[Judi Love]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Great British Bake Off spin-off revamp as Extra Slice is axed - with Jo Brand and Tom Allen exiting |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a73616728/great-british-bake-off-extra-slice-axed/ |website=[[Digital Spy]] |access-date=8 September 2026 |date=4 September 2026}}</ref> The series is set to begin on 22 September 2026.<ref>{{cite web |title=Bake Off 2026 start date revealed – plus, the baking kit worthy of star bakers |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/extras/indybest/gadgets-tech/television/great-british-bake-off-2026-kitchen-appliances-baking-essentials-b3046372.html |website=[[The Independent]] |access-date=8 September 2026 |language=en |date=8 September 2026}}</ref> 

== Bakers ==
